  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Vermont recorded $374M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state received 4,659 awards with an average award size of $80.3K. Obligations fell 57.3% year over year. The Department of Defense was the largest buyer, obligating $227M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $59.6M and the Department of Homeland Security with $42M. GLOBALFOUNDRIES U.S. 2 LLC was the largest contractor at $87.5M, and Semiconductor and Related Device Manufacturing led industries with $87.5M. Historical fiscal-year obligations show variation: FY21 was $394M, FY22 was $506M, FY23 was $424M, FY24 was $920M, and FY25 was $877M. FY2026 to date totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. This snapshot shows concentrated Department of Defense buying, a top vendor tied to semiconductor manufacturing, and a much smaller fiscal-year-to-date total versus recent full fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2026 to date totaled $374M. FY25 totaled $877M and FY24 totaled $920M. Fiscal-year obligations also were $394M in FY21, $506M in FY22, and $424M in FY23, and FY2026 to date totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors are the largest in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $227M, the largest buying agency. GLOBALFOUNDRIES U.S. 2 LLC received $87.5M and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION received $49.3M. Semiconductor and Related Device Manufacturing led industries with $87.5M in obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
